1
00:00:11,344 --> 00:00:12,512
Okay.

2
00:00:12,595 --> 00:00:15,348
- One, two…
- One two…

3
00:00:16,975 --> 00:00:19,019
<i>- My family.</i>
- Make lots of money, Dad!

4
00:00:19,102 --> 00:00:21,396
<i>As a child,</i>
we <i>were a common, middle-class family.</i>

5
00:00:21,479 --> 00:00:22,439
Oh my!

6
00:00:25,650 --> 00:00:26,776
<i>An ordinary family…</i>

7
00:00:28,153 --> 00:00:29,029
Can you move aside?

8
00:00:29,112 --> 00:00:31,406
<i>…that went bankrupt</i>
<i>after cosigning a loan.</i>

9
00:00:32,532 --> 00:00:35,869
<i>My dad, devastated by the unchanging debt</i>
<i>despite repayment,</i>

10
00:00:37,245 --> 00:00:40,206
<i>one day disappeared,</i>
<i>after saying he had found a good job.</i>

11
00:00:41,708 --> 00:00:43,209
<i>And the three of us remaining</i>

12
00:00:44,711 --> 00:00:46,337
<i>moved from one studio to the next.</i>

13
00:00:48,840 --> 00:00:51,468
<i>Every sleepless night,</i>
<i>I thought about the TV show</i>

14
00:00:52,844 --> 00:00:57,015
<i>that featured my whole family.</i>
A Father's Miracle.

15
00:00:57,098 --> 00:00:59,809
<i>Here comes the family.</i>
<i>A big round of applause, please.</i>

16
00:00:59,893 --> 00:01:01,436
<i>Yes.</i>

17
00:01:01,519 --> 00:01:04,272
<i>The father almost succeeded</i>
<i>in the last challenge.</i>

18
00:01:05,065 --> 00:01:05,899
<i>Although…</i>

19
00:01:05,982 --> 00:01:07,609
<i>Do you think your dad will succeed?</i>

20
00:01:07,692 --> 00:01:09,152
<i>…it wasn't really a good memory.</i>

21
00:01:09,235 --> 00:01:12,572
<i>Yes, I hope he succeeds.</i>
<i>I really hope he does!</i>

22
00:01:13,281 --> 00:01:16,159
<i>Today's challenge</i>
<i>for </i>A Father's Miracle <i>is</i>…

23
00:01:16,242 --> 00:01:18,787
<i>Juggling for ten seconds</i>
<i>while riding a unicycle.</i>

24
00:01:18,870 --> 00:01:21,998
<i>Will the father succeed</i>
<i>in achieving a miracle?</i>

25
00:01:22,082 --> 00:01:25,794
The father mounts the unicycle.

26
00:01:26,503 --> 00:01:28,505
This is a tense moment.

27
00:01:32,217 --> 00:01:33,802
- And he lets go.
- Yes.

28
00:01:33,885 --> 00:01:36,471
- And now…
- He's balancing and now has to juggle.

29
00:01:36,554 --> 00:01:38,640
- You can do it, sir.
- And from here…

30
00:01:38,723 --> 00:01:39,557
Oh no!

31
00:01:40,975 --> 00:01:42,185
Goodness, he fell.

32
00:01:42,268 --> 00:01:43,269
Oh no, sir!

33
00:01:43,353 --> 00:01:46,064
Sadly, today's <i>A Father's Miracle</i>
ends in failure.

34
00:01:46,147 --> 00:01:47,148
<i>Is that where it began?</i>

35
00:01:47,232 --> 00:01:48,316
Yes.

36
00:01:48,399 --> 00:01:49,317
<i>The moment my dad…</i>

37
00:01:49,400 --> 00:01:50,235
No, he fell again.

38
00:01:50,318 --> 00:01:52,403
<i>…began searching for sweet deal jobs.</i>

39
00:02:08,628 --> 00:02:12,632
<i>If I hadn't sent in a request</i>
<i>to be on the show…</i>

40
00:02:15,218 --> 00:02:16,719
<i>would things have been different?</i>

41
00:03:13,359 --> 00:03:17,113
DEAD-END JOB

42
00:03:18,281 --> 00:03:21,242
THE WALLS DON'T TALK

43
00:03:23,578 --> 00:03:24,579
<i>You don't think</i>

44
00:03:25,496 --> 00:03:28,583
Spider Staffing Agency
only deals with you, do you?

45
00:03:29,209 --> 00:03:32,003
You won't find a sweeter gig than this.

46
00:03:35,006 --> 00:03:36,424
That job

47
00:03:37,717 --> 00:03:39,510
is a sweet deal.

48
00:03:52,482 --> 00:03:57,320
LOOK RIGHT IF YOU'RE NOT BUSY

49
00:03:59,405 --> 00:04:00,531
Damn it.

50
00:04:01,699 --> 00:04:03,826
Fancy seeing you here.

51
00:04:04,994 --> 00:04:07,163
What are you doing here?

52
00:04:07,247 --> 00:04:09,540
I was passing by and saw you,
Mr. Hyeok-jun.

53
00:04:09,624 --> 00:04:11,542
You were just passing by?

54
00:04:14,921 --> 00:04:16,714
It's nice to see you here.

55
00:04:19,717 --> 00:04:23,096
I've met quite a few part-timers
in my time.

56
00:04:23,596 --> 00:04:26,808
And sometimes, in this line of work,

57
00:04:27,308 --> 00:04:30,561
there are people like you
who have a knack for this stuff.

58
00:04:31,646 --> 00:04:34,649
Usually, they give up or disappear
after one or two tries.

59
00:04:34,732 --> 00:04:37,485
What do you mean, disappear?

60
00:04:39,404 --> 00:04:42,031
I'm saying you're a natural at this.

61
00:04:43,157 --> 00:04:46,035
How did you think of going
to the Yangcheon Bio Clinic?

62
00:04:46,536 --> 00:04:47,495
What?

63
00:04:50,123 --> 00:04:52,250
And how did you escape
the milk delivery job?

64
00:04:54,711 --> 00:04:56,337
It's as if someone helped you.

65
00:04:58,047 --> 00:05:00,550
Well, you see, how should I…

66
00:05:00,633 --> 00:05:02,593
The penalty fee!

67
00:05:04,846 --> 00:05:07,849
You said there's a penalty fee
if I talk about the jobs.

68
00:05:08,891 --> 00:05:10,768
Is that why you're here?

69
00:05:12,520 --> 00:05:15,189
No, I've just developed
an interest in you.

70
00:05:16,190 --> 00:05:18,526
You left the milk delivery
without permission

71
00:05:19,027 --> 00:05:22,780
and took someone else's job
at the Yangcheon Bio Clinic.

72
00:05:23,281 --> 00:05:24,574
All without pay.

73
00:05:25,074 --> 00:05:28,036
I can't let a talent like you slip away.

74
00:05:30,204 --> 00:05:31,664
- Right?
- Sir.

75
00:05:32,206 --> 00:05:34,292
Can I ask you something?

76
00:05:35,501 --> 00:05:36,336
Sure.

77
00:05:37,712 --> 00:05:39,172
Do you know

78
00:05:40,757 --> 00:05:42,675
someone named Byeon Min-su

79
00:05:44,260 --> 00:05:45,219
by any chance?

80
00:05:48,556 --> 00:05:49,682
Byeon Min-su?

81
00:05:52,143 --> 00:05:53,686
Byeon Min-su…

82
00:05:55,313 --> 00:05:57,273
Byeon Min-su…

83
00:05:58,483 --> 00:05:59,984
Byeon Min-su…

84
00:06:05,907 --> 00:06:07,158
I don't think so.

85
00:06:11,162 --> 00:06:12,163
Now.

86
00:06:16,459 --> 00:06:18,544
Mr. Hyeok-jun, let's see how far

87
00:06:19,545 --> 00:06:20,380
you can go.

88
00:06:20,880 --> 00:06:23,800
- No, I'm done with the part-time jobs--
- Think it over slowly.

89
00:06:23,883 --> 00:06:25,802
You don't have to decide today.

90
00:06:27,387 --> 00:06:29,097
Just get through the day.

91
00:06:29,597 --> 00:06:30,807
You need to make money.

92
00:06:38,189 --> 00:06:41,442
FIRE HOT TTEOKBOKKI

93
00:06:47,824 --> 00:06:48,658
Hey.

94
00:06:49,325 --> 00:06:51,202
What brings you two here together?

95
00:06:51,285 --> 00:06:53,079
No reason. Hyeok-jun wanted to see you.

96
00:06:53,579 --> 00:06:54,831
- Really?
- Yeah.

97
00:06:55,331 --> 00:06:57,208
He could've just video-called me.

98
00:06:57,291 --> 00:06:59,043
I guess he was too shy to say so.

99
00:06:59,585 --> 00:07:02,505
Mom, just don't say anything
and take care of him for a few days.

100
00:07:03,923 --> 00:07:05,508
Why?

101
00:07:08,386 --> 00:07:12,014
I had a feeling
the interview wouldn't go well. Gosh.

102
00:07:12,098 --> 00:07:13,933
- Me?
- What?

103
00:07:16,144 --> 00:07:20,648
- Byeon Hyeok-jun had an interview?
- Oh, right. How did yours go?

104
00:08:18,289 --> 00:08:20,041
"Money to pay back"?

105
00:08:20,124 --> 00:08:22,251
UNCLE CHEOL-I 150,000 BY MID APR
SANG-WOO 190,000 BY APR

106
00:08:22,335 --> 00:08:24,337
SANG-MIN 180,000 BY EARLY AUG
MI-GYEONG 320,000 BY DEC

107
00:08:38,559 --> 00:08:41,187
"Tunnel construction, 50 times."

108
00:08:42,438 --> 00:08:44,524
"Quarry, 100 times."

109
00:08:45,399 --> 00:08:47,777
"Construction site, 200 times"?

110
00:08:48,861 --> 00:08:49,946
"The last."

111
00:08:51,030 --> 00:08:52,031
"The last…"

112
00:09:00,581 --> 00:09:03,084
"Construction site, night shift."

113
00:09:04,669 --> 00:09:06,212
"Construction site."

114
00:09:06,963 --> 00:09:08,214
"Day-night shift."

115
00:09:32,405 --> 00:09:37,785
ACCEPT

116
00:09:50,756 --> 00:09:52,633
BYEON JI-YOON
DID YOU TAKE ANOTHER PART-TIME JOB?

117
00:09:52,717 --> 00:09:54,176
GET YOUR ASS BACK HOME BEFORE I KILL…

118
00:09:54,260 --> 00:09:55,428
MISSED CALL
BYEON JI-YOON

119
00:10:07,106 --> 00:10:08,274
Mr. Byeon Hyeok-jun?

120
00:10:10,109 --> 00:10:12,028
Yes, that's me.

121
00:10:12,111 --> 00:10:14,196
A young fellow, I see. Hop in.

122
00:10:18,159 --> 00:10:19,452
What are you doing? Get in.

123
00:10:20,661 --> 00:10:21,621
Okay.

124
00:10:50,524 --> 00:10:52,401
Okay, let's get out.

125
00:10:58,074 --> 00:10:58,908
Ouch.

126
00:10:59,617 --> 00:11:01,202
Ow, my back.

127
00:11:03,287 --> 00:11:07,375
- What are you doing? Come here.
- I hope we can finish before nightfall.

128
00:11:08,918 --> 00:11:12,046
Today, we do cleanup
and nothing else. Got it?

129
00:11:12,129 --> 00:11:14,382
- Yes, cleanup!
- Cleanup!

130
00:11:14,465 --> 00:11:16,008
Everyone, stay focused.

131
00:11:22,348 --> 00:11:24,475
Start by quickly removing these supports.

132
00:11:24,558 --> 00:11:25,768
- Yes, sir.
- Yes, sir!

133
00:11:26,268 --> 00:11:28,604
- Hey, move it over here.
- Yes, sir.

134
00:11:28,688 --> 00:11:31,399
- Hurry up, rookie.
- There's no time, so hurry up!

135
00:11:31,482 --> 00:11:33,359
- Yes, hurry up!
- Yes, hurry up!

136
00:11:33,442 --> 00:11:35,528
- All right!
- Wait, what's that noise?

137
00:11:35,611 --> 00:11:38,322
- Remove this first.
- No, grab that side first.

138
00:11:38,406 --> 00:11:40,991
- Damn it! Everyone, get over here!
- Hurry up, people!

139
00:11:41,075 --> 00:11:42,284
We're running too late.

140
00:11:42,368 --> 00:11:43,786
What the hell is this?

141
00:11:44,286 --> 00:11:45,955
- What are you doing?
- What the hell?

142
00:11:46,038 --> 00:11:49,625
Why the hell are you removing
the supports we installed yesterday?

143
00:11:51,460 --> 00:11:53,796
What are you saying? Speak in Korean!

144
00:11:53,879 --> 00:11:55,381
"Speak in Korean!"

145
00:11:55,464 --> 00:11:57,717
What, are you going
to speak formally if I do?

146
00:11:57,800 --> 00:11:59,385
You bastard, you wanna die?

147
00:11:59,468 --> 00:12:01,554
Who ordered you to do this?

148
00:12:02,221 --> 00:12:04,181
We just need to remove the supports!

149
00:12:04,265 --> 00:12:05,641
- Hey, keep going!
- You bastard!

150
00:12:05,725 --> 00:12:09,061
Reinstall them now, bastard!
Are you going to be responsible for this?

151
00:12:09,145 --> 00:12:11,272
- Remove them all!
- No, stop that!

152
00:12:12,732 --> 00:12:15,276
Grab them!

153
00:12:15,359 --> 00:12:17,486
Get the fuck off me, bastard!

154
00:12:18,487 --> 00:12:19,613
You crazy bastard!

155
00:12:19,697 --> 00:12:22,283
Foreman, sir, no. Stop it!

156
00:12:22,366 --> 00:12:24,326
Who the hell are you? Move it!

157
00:12:29,415 --> 00:12:30,916
You're going to kill him!

158
00:12:31,000 --> 00:12:31,876
Let go!

159
00:12:59,028 --> 00:13:00,154
Hey, get a grip!

160
00:13:01,280 --> 00:13:02,490
We'll stop here.

161
00:13:02,573 --> 00:13:04,533
Get up. Let's go!

162
00:13:06,243 --> 00:13:07,536
Those damn bastards.

163
00:13:08,078 --> 00:13:10,080
You'll pay for this.

164
00:13:11,040 --> 00:13:12,708
Is everyone okay?

165
00:13:12,792 --> 00:13:14,543
Fucking bastards.

166
00:13:20,090 --> 00:13:22,134
Beware of your foreman.

167
00:13:26,597 --> 00:13:29,225
Now let's take down
the illegal banner on the outer wall.

168
00:13:29,308 --> 00:13:32,228
- You want to do that too?
- But there's no proper scaffolding.

169
00:13:33,145 --> 00:13:36,148
Like we ever had proper scaffolding.
Let's do it quickly and go.

170
00:13:36,899 --> 00:13:37,733
Hey, Kim.

171
00:13:38,234 --> 00:13:39,902
You take care of that side, okay?

172
00:13:39,985 --> 00:13:42,154
Man, that damn banner…

173
00:13:42,238 --> 00:13:43,072
Hey, rookie.

174
00:13:44,156 --> 00:13:44,990
Yes?

175
00:13:45,574 --> 00:13:48,911
- Did you play on the jungle gym as a kid?
- Sorry?

176
00:13:50,246 --> 00:13:52,623
Damn, this is one tall jungle gym.

177
00:13:54,708 --> 00:13:55,584
Oh shit.

178
00:14:00,381 --> 00:14:02,341
Relax, the safety hooks
will keep you safe.

179
00:14:09,765 --> 00:14:12,017
Latch the safety hook on the outside.

180
00:14:12,601 --> 00:14:14,520
That's it.

181
00:14:20,150 --> 00:14:20,985
Oh shit.

182
00:14:42,840 --> 00:14:44,633
Yeah, just cut that.

183
00:14:57,229 --> 00:15:00,274
"The price of 30 buried lives…

184
00:15:02,693 --> 00:15:04,486
will be repaid with death."

185
00:15:17,541 --> 00:15:19,418
Kim! Holy shit!

186
00:15:19,501 --> 00:15:21,587
What are you doing? Get down there, now!

187
00:15:22,087 --> 00:15:24,048
Hurry, go! Hurry!

188
00:15:24,840 --> 00:15:26,091
Fuck.

189
00:15:26,842 --> 00:15:29,887
Hang in there, brother.
The ambulance is on its way.

190
00:15:29,970 --> 00:15:31,555
It's almost here.

191
00:15:32,264 --> 00:15:33,933
- Just hang in there.
- Wait. What…

192
00:15:34,433 --> 00:15:37,561
- What is it?
- That bastard's sending it away.

193
00:15:38,771 --> 00:15:39,980
No, over here!

194
00:15:41,023 --> 00:15:42,566
What the hell are you doing?

195
00:15:43,192 --> 00:15:45,152
Why'd you send it away, bastard?

196
00:15:47,112 --> 00:15:48,447
- Who the hell are you?
- What?

197
00:15:49,281 --> 00:15:51,533
This bastard sent the ambulance away!
Damn it!

198
00:15:53,160 --> 00:15:54,578
You crazy bastard!

199
00:15:55,204 --> 00:15:56,163
Can't you see he's hurt?

200
00:15:57,665 --> 00:16:00,584
I was told not to let the ambulance in.

201
00:16:01,085 --> 00:16:02,711
You transport anyone who gets hurt.

202
00:16:02,795 --> 00:16:04,338
What's up with this bastard?

203
00:16:04,922 --> 00:16:06,006
Are you a Koryoin?

204
00:16:06,090 --> 00:16:07,299
Just get back to work.

205
00:16:07,383 --> 00:16:08,258
Goddammit!

206
00:16:08,801 --> 00:16:10,344
Look, you fucking bastard.

207
00:16:10,427 --> 00:16:13,639
Can't you see a man's about to die?

208
00:16:14,139 --> 00:16:17,601
Come on. Don't pretend
like you don't fucking know!

209
00:16:17,685 --> 00:16:18,644
You knew all along.

210
00:16:18,727 --> 00:16:20,771
No? But you did.

211
00:16:20,854 --> 00:16:23,357
Are you saying you didn't?
But you did know.

212
00:16:23,983 --> 00:16:25,317
Stop it.

213
00:16:26,735 --> 00:16:30,447
- Calm down.
- How the fuck do we work like this?

214
00:16:35,119 --> 00:16:36,078
What are you saying?

215
00:16:36,161 --> 00:16:38,330
The ambulance was sent away.

216
00:16:38,831 --> 00:16:40,290
What, do you expect us all to die?

217
00:16:41,834 --> 00:16:45,004
Did I send it away?
Why are you guys making a fuss too?

218
00:16:45,087 --> 00:16:49,425
- This isn't what you fucking promised us!
- What promise?

219
00:16:50,259 --> 00:16:51,093
Hey!

220
00:16:51,885 --> 00:16:55,931
Did any of you fucks come here
not knowing how dangerous it was?

221
00:16:57,349 --> 00:16:59,309
Goddammit. Fucking hell.

222
00:17:00,144 --> 00:17:01,562
That's not it!

223
00:17:02,479 --> 00:17:06,650
Maybe you can pull that on others,
but not with us, damn it!

224
00:17:07,359 --> 00:17:11,405
We don't plan on dying here,
so go find someone else.

225
00:17:11,488 --> 00:17:13,282
Go get the van now to load him up!

226
00:17:13,907 --> 00:17:15,784
- Hey.
- Yes?

227
00:17:16,410 --> 00:17:17,536
What about you?

228
00:17:18,328 --> 00:17:20,914
I have to stay until the end…

229
00:17:23,417 --> 00:17:24,460
Fucking hell.

230
00:17:24,543 --> 00:17:25,377
Hey!

231
00:17:26,920 --> 00:17:30,132
Bunch of weak-willed bastards!
See if I ever hire you again!

232
00:17:32,676 --> 00:17:34,053
Rookie, you'll stay, right?

233
00:17:36,180 --> 00:17:37,389
Yes.

234
00:17:37,890 --> 00:17:38,724
Okay.

235
00:17:39,391 --> 00:17:41,226
The two of us can finish the rest.

236
00:17:45,856 --> 00:17:46,732
Ah shit.

237
00:17:48,192 --> 00:17:49,109
Hurry up.

238
00:17:58,660 --> 00:18:01,371
- Let's put that down and take a break.
- Yes.

239
00:18:12,925 --> 00:18:14,384
So are there always

240
00:18:15,761 --> 00:18:17,638
a lot of accidents on site?

241
00:18:17,721 --> 00:18:19,348
Buildings don't just get built.

242
00:18:20,349 --> 00:18:22,726
They're built on blood and bones.

243
00:18:26,146 --> 00:18:27,481
Especially this one.

244
00:18:28,357 --> 00:18:29,566
Building…

245
00:18:34,947 --> 00:18:38,450
Are you interested in this work?
Do you want to officially join our team?

246
00:18:38,951 --> 00:18:41,829
You're not the best worker,
but you have a sense of desperation.

247
00:18:41,912 --> 00:18:42,830
That's enough.

248
00:18:43,831 --> 00:18:46,500
I appreciate the offer, but I…

249
00:18:47,000 --> 00:18:49,086
Hey, even people
with physical issues do this.

250
00:18:52,589 --> 00:18:54,758
Job sites always have a few like that.

251
00:18:55,425 --> 00:18:57,511
We had one on our team too, named Byeon.

252
00:19:00,556 --> 00:19:02,850
Byeon?

253
00:19:04,393 --> 00:19:07,062
Despite his physical issue
and the constant chewing out,

254
00:19:07,146 --> 00:19:08,105
he refused to quit.

255
00:19:08,689 --> 00:19:10,482
Honestly, he was a nuisance.

256
00:19:11,525 --> 00:19:13,402
In the end, he met a bad end on-site.

257
00:19:14,903 --> 00:19:17,656
The man you just mentioned, Byeon,

258
00:19:18,448 --> 00:19:19,366
his fingers…

259
00:19:20,701 --> 00:19:22,536
Did he have all ten?

260
00:19:24,121 --> 00:19:24,955
Well…

261
00:19:26,832 --> 00:19:29,084
I think he might have been
missing a couple.

262
00:19:35,674 --> 00:19:37,926
If not, he couldn't have been
that bad at his job.

263
00:19:41,013 --> 00:19:42,723
Let's move to the basement.

264
00:19:43,265 --> 00:19:44,391
We're almost done now.

265
00:19:45,017 --> 00:19:48,061
We both need to make money
to get back to our families.

266
00:19:52,399 --> 00:19:53,525
Grab that and follow me.

267
00:20:02,242 --> 00:20:03,994
- Watch your step.
- Okay.

268
00:20:10,083 --> 00:20:11,168
Turn off the light!

269
00:20:15,464 --> 00:20:17,674
All the dust down here
could cause an explosion.

270
00:20:18,342 --> 00:20:19,551
The lighting junction box.

271
00:20:20,052 --> 00:20:21,136
I see.

272
00:20:36,109 --> 00:20:37,361
Put that over there.

273
00:20:37,444 --> 00:20:39,029
Then I'll stack them inside.

274
00:20:39,112 --> 00:20:40,530
- Okay.
- All right.

275
00:21:09,601 --> 00:21:10,519
Let's stop here.

276
00:21:12,813 --> 00:21:14,147
Okay.

277
00:21:14,690 --> 00:21:16,024
All right, good work.

278
00:21:16,108 --> 00:21:17,693
Looks like it's about time too.

279
00:21:17,776 --> 00:21:18,610
Let's go.

280
00:21:20,654 --> 00:21:21,697
Well, but…

281
00:22:51,620 --> 00:22:52,621
You were curious, huh?

282
00:22:56,833 --> 00:22:59,336
Why the work we do here
doesn't make sense?

283
00:23:05,342 --> 00:23:07,344
Because accidents must happen.

284
00:23:08,303 --> 00:23:10,514
This crazy building devours people.

285
00:23:13,058 --> 00:23:15,268
They say a shaman told them
at the site selection

286
00:23:16,269 --> 00:23:17,854
to build a tower of human bones.

287
00:23:19,773 --> 00:23:22,859
That they need 100 human sacrifices
to ensure wealth for generations.

288
00:23:24,152 --> 00:23:25,404
I don't want to do it.

289
00:23:27,239 --> 00:23:30,492
But they give me a lot of money
to do this.

290
00:23:32,452 --> 00:23:33,703
That's why you're here too.

291
00:23:36,206 --> 00:23:39,292
In any case, we survived today.

292
00:23:39,876 --> 00:23:41,461
We just need to get paid.

293
00:23:41,545 --> 00:23:42,712
We're not to blame.

294
00:23:44,673 --> 00:23:45,674
Right?

295
00:24:21,585 --> 00:24:23,587
Only fools end up dead, damn it.

296
00:24:24,087 --> 00:24:25,881
Is making a living a crime?

297
00:24:29,050 --> 00:24:30,844
Is surviving a crime, damn it?

298
00:25:04,419 --> 00:25:06,755
- Did you do that to all the workers here?
- No!

299
00:25:06,838 --> 00:25:09,049
People like that Byeon guy?

300
00:25:09,883 --> 00:25:11,426
Did you do that to all of them?

301
00:25:11,510 --> 00:25:14,304
Byeon? What are you talking about?

302
00:25:14,387 --> 00:25:17,224
That Byeon guy from earlier.
What was his name?

303
00:25:17,307 --> 00:25:20,185
I don't know.
Everyone just called him Byeon.

304
00:25:20,268 --> 00:25:21,269
You don't remember?

305
00:25:22,270 --> 00:25:24,856
You don't remember his name
after telling me all of that?

306
00:25:24,940 --> 00:25:26,274
Byeon Min-su!

307
00:25:29,528 --> 00:25:30,695
Byeon.

308
00:25:30,779 --> 00:25:31,863
Byeon Min-su.

309
00:25:38,745 --> 00:25:39,913
Did you kill him?

310
00:25:41,414 --> 00:25:42,249
No.

311
00:25:43,375 --> 00:25:45,293
- Did you kill him and…
- No!

312
00:25:45,377 --> 00:25:46,878
No, Byeon isn't buried there.

313
00:25:46,962 --> 00:25:48,004
I'm certain of that.

314
00:25:49,214 --> 00:25:50,799
What?

315
00:25:51,299 --> 00:25:52,717
Byeon isn't dead.

316
00:25:52,801 --> 00:25:54,135
He disappeared.

317
00:25:54,719 --> 00:25:55,679
While working.

318
00:25:56,846 --> 00:25:57,889
Where did he go?

319
00:25:59,641 --> 00:26:01,351
Where the hell did he go?

320
00:26:01,434 --> 00:26:02,644
I don't know…

321
00:26:05,689 --> 00:26:06,898
where he went.

322
00:26:08,858 --> 00:26:10,402
He went through a door

323
00:26:11,611 --> 00:26:12,946
and never came back.

324
00:26:18,326 --> 00:26:20,787
He should be somewhere.

325
00:27:03,330 --> 00:27:10,337
YOUR FAMILY HOPES
FOR YOUR SAFETY TODAY TOO

326
00:27:10,420 --> 00:27:16,593
<i>The sewing machine spins so well</i>
<i>It goes on spinning</i>

327
00:27:19,262 --> 00:27:25,769
<i>Red flowers, yellow flowers</i>
<i>Even when the garden is in full bloom</i>

328
00:27:27,729 --> 00:27:34,235
<i>White butterflies, flower butterflies</i>
<i>Even when they flutter over the wall</i>

329
00:31:49,032 --> 00:31:52,452
Subtitle translation by:
